# Practical 2 – Selection Sort

## Aim
To implement Selection Sort in Python and analyze its time complexity.

## Description
Selection Sort repeatedly finds the smallest element from the unsorted part of the list and places it at the correct position.

## Input
```text
Enter numbers separated by spaces: 5 7 2 1 8 4 6
````

## Output

```text
Original list: [5, 7, 2, 1, 8, 4, 6]
Sorted list (Selection Sort): [1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]
Time Complexity: O(n^2)
Execution Time: 0.000013 seconds
```

## Complexity

* Best Case: O(n²)
* Average Case: O(n²)
* Worst Case: O(n²)
* Space Complexity: O(1)

## Conclusion

Selection Sort is a simple sorting algorithm that repeatedly selects the smallest element and places it in the correct position.

